{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 41, :comments ["<b>Let the days of mourning for my father draw near.</b> He hung the matter on the days of mourning, because a mourner is forbidden to engage in Torah, as it says: ״פִּקּוּדֵי ה׳ יְשָׁרִים מְשַׂמְּחֵי לֵב״ (Psalms 19:9), and Yitzhak said: ״וְהָיָה כַּאֲשֶׁר תָּרִיד״ (Genesis 27:40) — that is, at a time when they do not engage in Torah, ״וּפָרַקְתָּ עֻלּוֹ״ (ibid.) — and if so, during his mourning he will certainly not engage in Torah and he will have nothing that shields him, and then ״אַהַרְגָה אֶת אָחִי״ (Genesis 27:41). And for this reason our Rabbis of blessed memory said (Berakhot 44b) that a mourner requires guarding, because the Torah that shields him is not within him, as it is written (Proverbs 6:22): ״בְּהִתְהַלֶּכְךָ תַּנְחֶה אֹתָךְ, בְּשָׁכְבְּךָ תִּשְׁמֹר עָלֶיךָ״."], :book :genesis, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:30:42.583190404Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}